{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793372702,"nonce":"6C6hUojWrBbYhKWzc8/bSMhqqxc=","message":"Design survey (2026-10-30), shared by this issue and Tw completion 56b5e8550a868f7d1e417e221a9d5992af82450a389c6e51c43a22c3cf551ebc.\n\nWhere Rayzor stands (HEAD 6a641f2f)\n- Triggers are only \".\" and \":\" (lsp/src/server.rs:125). The only context classifier is analysis::receiver_before (analysis.rs:1115); \":\" is advertised but unclassified. Items carry no textEdit, range, filterText or snippet (server.rs:1223). The cached Names answer is rendered once at 0:0, so it is position-independent (server.rs:855).\n- Inline markup is one MarkupLit token (parser/src/token.rs:41, markup.rs). An unterminated tag, quote or `{` is a LexError that fails tokenization of the whole file, and the strict rd_parse gate (context.rs:376) then keeps the last analysis. Nothing token-level survives inside markup while it is being typed.\n- Unverified: on a syntactically broken document, declaration_snapshot returns no declarations (workspace_index.rs:380) and is published as a partial before compile (server.rs:767), so non-receiver completion may be answered from that empty cached snapshot. Check before building on it.\n- No channel exists for a library to give the LSP data. Macros already run under the LSP (typecheck_only, preview budget, deferred build), and generated markup classes already resolve for hover/definition (references.rs:91, fixture session.rs:4769).\n\nWhere Ashui stands (HEAD 1146207)\n- Tags: Hxx.lowerNode/lowerComponent with private static tables TEXT_TAGS, BOX_TAGS, FLOW_TAGS, BUILT_IN_CLASSES plus hard-coded div/pre/text/svg/img; imported non-ashui.ui components shadow built-ins except div; module sub-types resolve (`\u003cdialog-trigger\u003e` from Dialog).\n- Attributes: per-tag rules in lowerDiv/setter/lowerComponent; layout attributes are the statics of ashui.layout.Prop (bg -\u003e Background); HANDLERS map to event types; DSL forms if/else/for.\n- Props: componentProps walks superclasses to Component and takes params[0] without applying type parameters, so a generic intermediate base yields the raw parameter.\n- Tw: the vocabulary map `known` is private; transform, motion, gradient, backdrop, keyword, glass, opacity-suffix and clip-path families are regex or inline tables, not in the map. Variants come from STATES (@:noCompletion), one per class.\n- CSS: DeclaredCss.include is order-dependent; the blinc-css manifest gives classes and imports but no selector spans.\n- Markup.displayed already gives Haxe --display completion inside `{expr}`; no tag/attribute/class completion exists.\n\nProposed design\n1. Provider channel. A library marks the entry point that owns a syntax with plain metadata naming a provider class, e.g. `@:ide.completion(\"ashui.ide.HxxCompletion\")` on ashui.ui.Markup.build (inline markup) and on Hxx.hxx and Tw.tw (string forms). Plain metadata is inert under haxe and needs no rayzor package. Rayzor finds the provider through the entry point it already resolved: for a call, the callee's typed identity, never an arbitrary function named tw; for an @:markup literal, the global build macro that consumed it, recorded when the macro ran.\n2. Provider contract. Macro-context static functions returning plain descriptors `{label, kind, detail, doc, insert, snippet?}` for a query `{context, tag?, attribute?, present:Array\u003cString\u003e, prefix}`. The provider answers the library's own vocabulary and rules (built-in tags, shadowing, root attributes, handlers, DSL forms, Tw words/variants, authored CSS classes). For component props it returns a rule, \"params[0] of the superclass chain up to ashui.ui.Component\", and Rayzor evaluates it with its typer, substituting generic parameters, which also fixes the componentProps gap above.\n3. Rayzor context. A tolerant markup scanner over the raw text around the cursor (reusing parser/src/markup.rs) classifies tag name (open/close), attribute name, quoted attribute value, string argument of a provider callee, or Haxe expression (handled by existing completion), and yields the replacement range. Unterminated markup becomes a recoverable error token, so the rest of the file keeps parsing.\n4. Protocol. textEdit ranges replacing only the current token, snippets for tags and arbitrary values, triggers `\u003c` `/` space `\"` `-` `:` with context filtering so comparisons and ordinary strings get nothing.\n5. Cache. Provider results keyed by provider identity, query, defines, library revision, compiler BUILD_ID and the module dependencies the provider registers (stylesheets via registerModuleDependency), stored beside the editor snapshot; served before full indexing; dropped by generation like other partials.\n\nOrder\n1. Rayzor items 3 and 4 with a portable fixture provider in lsp/tests (no Ashui), then 1, 2 and 5.\n2. Ashui: HxxCompletion over the existing tables; Tw exposes an enumeration built from the same tables the parser uses, with a test that every offered word parses; DeclaredCss exposes its catalog.\n3. blinc-css manifest gains selector spans for CSS docs and go-to-definition.","files":null}]}